# ref-9e5a4cd-allocator-neutral
# A 5-box stack on a flat ground box, 60 steps at fixed dt=1/60, 4 substeps, no wall
# clock.
# The allocator API widening (b3AllocFcn size_t, b3FreeFcn + size, b3GetByteCount
# int64_t) is not a simulation observable; this scene pins that simulation results are
# unchanged: the stack's resting height and its contact count after 60 steps must agree
# with vanilla float box3d at upstream commit 9e5a4cd within tolerance.
# Reference: vanilla float box3d at upstream commit 9e5a4cd.
# Fixed: fixed3d on this branch (allocator widening ported). The engine is Q48.16 fixed
#   point with the exact-SAT structure and no float SIMD hull core, so traces are not
#   bit-identical to float; the stack must settle to the same configuration within
#   tolerance.
# Observable: the highest box's resting y and the world's contact count after 60 steps.
# Tolerance: resting height within 0.05 m and contact count equal, stated as twice the
#   measured maximum divergence once the reference harness (tools/reference/, from card
#   fixed3d-box3d-reference-harness) is present at the base; that harness is absent at
#   BASE sprint/fixed3d-box3d-ports, so this scene is added for its glob and the
#   ctest -L reference run is reported not-done in the port record until it lands.
scene ref-9e5a4cd-allocator-neutral
body box half 10 0.5 10 position 0 -0.5 0 static
body box half 0.5 0.5 0.5 position 0 0.5 0 density 1.0
body box half 0.5 0.5 0.5 position 0 1.5 0 density 1.0
body box half 0.5 0.5 0.5 position 0 2.5 0 density 1.0
body box half 0.5 0.5 0.5 position 0 3.5 0 density 1.0
body box half 0.5 0.5 0.5 position 0 4.5 0 density 1.0
steps 60 dt 1/60 substeps 4
expect contactCount >= 4
expect restingY > 3.5
